The source document, NASA Technical Memorandum 100991 (Ballin, 1988), included
here as docs/ballin-tm100991.pdf, is a work of the United States Government
prepared by an officer or employee as part of that person's official duties, and
is therefore not subject to copyright protection in the United States under
17 U.S.C. section 105. It is not covered by the licence above.

Two qualifications, both checkable on the face of the document:

  * Section 105 removes copyright IN THE UNITED STATES only. The United States
    government may hold or receive copyright in the document abroad, and this
    repository makes no claim about its status outside the United States.

  * Section 105 covers works OF the government. The report reproduces material
    from at least one work that is not: Figure 2 [pdf p.18] is captioned "(From
    ref. 6.)", and reference 6 [pdf p.102] is

        Prescott, W. E.; and Mabee, R. L.: T700-GE-700 Training Guide.
        General Electric Aircraft Engine Business Group; Technical Training
        Operation, 1984.

    a General Electric publication. Reference 4 is a United Technologies
    Sikorsky Aircraft report (SER-70982) and reference 5 a General Electric
    model specification. Nothing in this repository is derived from Figure 2 --
    it is a cutaway illustration of the engine, and no number is taken from it --
    but the blanket sentence "the source document is in the public domain" was
    over-broad and is corrected here rather than left standing.
